judge_raw_output:
The analyzer shows early but narrow performance gains (mean performance 0.0527, std 0.0016, max 0.0548) alongside collapsed diversity (distance_from_center mean 0.2926, std 0.0101, down from 0.0450). This looks like premature convergence due to insufficient exploration incentives. Add the registered parameter_spread objective (weight comparable to distance_from_center) to encourage broader phenotypic diversity.

<decision>
{
  "failure_location": "objective",
  "root_cause_hypothesis": "Exploration objectives are insufficiently incentivized: distance_from_center (weight 0.25) has not prevented clustering (std dropped from 0.0450 to 0.0101) and no parameter_spread objective is present, so the optimizer is prematurely exploiting a narrow region.",
  "intervention_target": "objective",
  "rationale": "Performance improved from ~0.0004 to mean=0.0527 (std=0.0016) but the population shows a tight performance spread (range ~0.011) and reduced diversity (distance_from_center mean=0.2926, std=0.0101). Adding parameter_spread (registered scorer) with weight comparable to distance_from_center should push the search to explore more varied parameter combinations and help escape local clustering.",
  "proposed_change": {
    "ops": [
      {
        "op": "add_from_registry",
        "name": "parameter_spread",
        "optimization_direction": "maximize",
        "weight": 0.25
      }
    ]
  },
  "expected_benefit": "Increase candidate-wise phenotypic diversity (std of parameters) and exploration of different regions, reducing premature convergence and increasing the chance of finding higher-performance designs.",
  "validation_plan": "After the change, monitor next 3 iterations for (a) an increase in diversity (parameter_spread std and distance_from_center std should rise from current ~0.01) and (b) improvement in best or mean performance beyond the current max 0.0548 or mean 0.0527. The independent validator will accept the change if it yields improved accepted-state metrics per its test.",
  "confidence": 0.75
}
</decision>

Analysis shows the population has zero objective variance (Analyzer: "every objective has zero population standard deviation"), performance is very low (performance mean = 0.0529 ±0.0000) and the two diversity objectives currently carry combined weight 0.25 + 0.35 = 0.60. That likely biases the optimizer toward diversity rather than exploiting the scarce performance gradient. As the Analyzer recommended, the next step should prioritize exploitation of performance to determine whether a performance gradient exists (vs. a deeper implementation/sampling bug). I will therefore increase the explicit weight on the performance objective so it becomes the dominant incentive for the next iterations.

<decision>
{
  "failure_location": "objective",
  "root_cause_hypothesis": "Conflicting objective weights: diversity objectives (parameter_spread weight=0.25 + distance_from_center weight=0.35 = 0.60) are dominating optimization pressure and preventing focus on improving performance; this likely causes stagnation (zero objective variance) and low performance mean=0.0529. Implementation/sampling bug is possible but secondary at this stage.",
  "intervention_target": "objective",
  "rationale": "All objectives show zero population std (Analyzer), performance remains very low (mean=0.0529 ±0.0000) while diversity objectives combined weight = 0.60. Temporarily making performance the dominant objective should allow exploitation and reveal whether a performance gradient exists before further changes or debugging.",
  "proposed_change": {
    "ops": [
      {
        "op": "set_weight",
        "name": "performance",
        "weight": 1.5
      }
    ]
  },
  "expected_benefit": "Shifts optimizer pressure toward improving performance (performance will have >~71% of weighted emphasis vs current diversity total), increasing chance to see objective variance and measurable performance gains if a gradient exists. If objective scores remain identical afterward, that will strengthen the evidence for an implementation/sampling bug.",
  "validation_plan": "Monitor next 2–5 iterations for (1) nonzero population std in objectives (objective std > 0), and (2) a rise in performance mean above 0.0529. If neither occurs, proceed to an implementation-targeted intervention (investigate candidate generation/evaluation).",
  "confidence": 0.62
}
</decision>
